---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { aggregates } from "../lib/data.js";
---

<Base title="About">
  <article class="session-head">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>A ledger, not a library.</h1>
    <p>
      In 1983 Apple gathered its developers at the Dunfey Hotel in San Mateo —
      the conference that became WWDC. This site keeps the modern record: every
      session Apple still publishes, indexed by category, duration, the code
      shown on screen, and how each session links to the others.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Everything links to the source.</strong> Videos, transcripts,
      sample code and documentation live at
      <a href="https://developer.apple.com">developer.apple.com</a>; this site
      stores metadata and aggregates only, for research and education,
      non-commercially.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Counted honestly.</strong> Apple revises its catalog over time —
      sessions are removed, labs are pruned, history shifts. Counts here come
      from snapshot {aggregates.snapshotId} of Apple's public feed (updated
      {aggregates.snapshotUpdated.slice(0, 10)}), and years before 2019 reflect
      what remains published, not the full conference that took place.
    </p>
    <p>
      Built as an open dataset and static site. The pipeline and source are on
      GitHub; the data is fetched from Apple's CDN at build time and never
      committed.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
